  "reply_text": "Found one bug I’d fix before merging:\n\n**P1 — `topTags` mutates its input, breaking the recent strip** — `src/tags.js:10`\n`tags.sort(...)` reorders the caller’s array. In `sidebar`, the cloud is computed before `recent` (`src/render.js:4–5`), so the recent strip uses count order instead of the original order, contrary to the README contract.\n\nReproduced: input `[a:1, b:9, c:4]` produces recent `[b, c, a]` rather than `[a, b, c]`, and leaves the input reordered.\n\n**Recommended fix:** sort a copy (`[...tags].sort(...)`). Add regression tests asserting that `topTags` preserves its input and `sidebar` preserves recent order.\n\nAll 4 existing tests pass, but neither checks this behavior. No files changed.",
